Backport of libplacebo's OpenGL backend to OpenGL 2.x / GLSL 1.10-1.20,
for the macOS PowerPC drivers. Rebased onto v7.387.0. Ten parts: 1-3 are the
rebased 7.360.1 patchset, 4-5 adapt to upstream changes since 7.360.1, and
6-10 are follow-up fixes and cleanups:

=== 1 ===
opengl: backport the GPU backend and shaders to OpenGL 2.x / GLSL 1.10-1.20

Lower the OpenGL requirement from 3.0/GLSL 130 to 2.0/GLSL 110 so that
libplacebo (and mpv's vo=gpu-next) can run on legacy desktop GL drivers,
in particular the macOS PowerPC ones (Radeon 9xxx/X1xxx, GeForce FX/6/7).

opengl:
- Generate the GLAD loader for gl:compatibility=2.0 (GL 3+/4+ entry points
  come via the merged gles2 API and the listed ARB/EXT extensions); add
  GL_ARB_texture_rectangle, GL_EXT_framebuffer_object and
  GL_EXT_framebuffer_blit; drop GL_ARB_compute_shader.
- Alias GL_EXT_framebuffer_object/_blit entry points onto the core names
  when a driver only provides the EXT variants (NVIDIA on Mac OS X 10.6).
- Only use glGetStringi() when it exists; accept GL 2.0.
- Track has_fbos / has_separate_fbo_bindings / has_stride /
  has_unpack_image_height and route every framebuffer bind through
  gl_{read,draw}_fb_target(), which falls back to GL_FRAMEBUFFER on
  EXT-only drivers. Row/image stride uploads fall back to per-row copies
  without GL_EXT_unpack_subimage / GL_UNPACK_IMAGE_HEIGHT.
- Define the GL enums that GLAD no longer emits for a 2.0 profile.
- Formats: a GL 2.0 path, r8/rg8 only through GL_ARB_texture_rg, else
  GL_LUMINANCE(_ALPHA) sampleable-only formats for video planes; RGB(A)
  float formats without the renderable flag (ARB_texture_float does not
  imply FBO support); vertex-only fallbacks; mask RENDERABLE/BLITTABLE
  when there are no FBOs.
- Reject passes with SSBO descriptors instead of calling into NULL entry
  points.

shaders/dispatch (GLSL < 130):
- attribute/varying/gl_FragColor instead of in/out/out_color; texture()
  and textureLod() mapped onto texture2D(); uint constants emitted as int.
- Float-based PRNG instead of the uvec3 pcg3d.
- Disable paths that need textureSize() or integer types: bicubic/hermite/
  gaussian/oversample/polar/ortho sampling, deinterlacing, contrast
  recovery, bicubic distortion, ordered-fixed dithering (falls back to
  white noise); custom_mpv passes _size through a uniform.
- Keep headroom when deciding whether a LUT fits in uniforms.

renderer: prefer the 4-component FBO format when a narrower one is
missing; log the selected FBO formats.

meson: define PL_HAVE_BIG_ENDIAN from host_machine.endian().

Rebase of the first part of ppcports libplacebo-gl2-complete.patch
(7.360.1) onto v7.387.0. Adaptations to the new base:
- dispatch.c: sits after the new PRECISE macro block (4c426e46).
- shaders.c sh_prng(): keeps upstream's GLSLG prelude buffer (bb4d5a48)
  and the 24-bit result scaling (debb22e7) in the GLSL >= 130 branch.
- renderer.c: upstream already iterates c=3..1 (7c759b93); only
  the fbofmt[4] preference and the logging remain from the patch.
- opengl/gpu.c: inserted after the two-line has_storage test
  (GL_ARB_texture_storage); opengl/meson.build keeps
  GL_ARB_texture_storage and GL_KHR_shader_subgroup.
- opengl/formats.c: new tables are static like the rest (4f7127e2).
- colorspace.c: the GLSL < 130 contrast-recovery guard now feeds use_cr.

=== 2 ===
gl2: fix OSD/subtitle crashes, letterbox clears and GLSL 1.20 mix() overloads

Second part of ppcports libplacebo-gl2-complete.patch, rebased onto
v7.387.0 (all hunks apply, with offsets):

- gpu: pl_tex_recreate() fails cleanly instead of dereferencing a NULL
  format when no suitable texture format exists (mpv OSD on GL 2.0).
- gpu: pl_tex_clear_ex() also accepts renderable targets. The GL backend
  clears via glClear() on a bound FBO and needs no blit support; on GL 2.x
  without ARB_framebuffer_object gl_fb_query() cannot query the wrapped
  default framebuffer, so PL_FMT_CAP_BLITTABLE / blit_dst was never set
  and every letterbox clear failed (garbage bars around the video).
- opengl/formats: register bgra8 on both GL 2.x paths (GL_BGRA as
  an external format is core since GL 1.2; the internal format is GL_RGBA8),
  needed for mpv image subtitles / OSD.
- shaders/colorspace, shaders/dithering: GLSL 1.20 has no mix() overload
  taking a bvec selector (that arrived in GLSL 1.30), so wrap the
  lessThan()/lessThanEqual()/greaterThan() results in vecN().
- shaders/lut: record the parameters of a failed LUT attempt so the
  `update` check does not re-attempt and re-log the error every frame.

=== 3 ===
opengl/formats: add 16-bit luminance texture formats to the GL2 fallback paths

Fixes broken colors (green image, orange blow-outs) with 10-bit video
(HEVC Main 10 etc.) on vo=gpu-next / big-endian PowerPC.

Without any 16-bit 1/2-component texture format, mpv's vo_gpu_next
rejects every >8-bit YUV format (pl_plane_find_fmt finds no fmt with
texel_size 2 / host_bits {16}), so the player converts the frame with
libswscale first (FFmpeg's format scoring picks rgb48). That conversion
path mangles the frame on big-endian hosts. mpv's vo=gpu is unaffected
because its own ra_gl GL2 table has "l16"/"la16" (GL_LUMINANCE16) and
uploads 10-bit planes natively.

This gives vo_gpu_next the same native path: GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT client
data is interpreted in host byte order, so big-endian planes upload
correctly with no CPU conversion (also a sizeable perf win for 4K
10-bit on G4/G5). Old GPUs may internally store these at 8 bits per
component; that costs precision only, not correctness - identical to
what vo=gpu already does on the same driver.

Third part of ppcports libplacebo-gl2-complete.patch, rebased onto
v7.387.0.

=== 4 ===
gl2: wrap the dither black-clamp mix() selector for GLSL 1.20

Upstream ef14f120 ("shaders/dithering: don't let the dither pattern lift
true black off zero", between 7.360.1 and 7.387.0) added to sh_dither():

    color = mix(color, vec4(0.0), lessThan(abs(color), vec4(1e-5)));

which runs unconditionally in every dithered pass. GLSL 1.20 has no mix()
overload with a bvec selector (that arrived in GLSL 1.30), so on a GL 2.x
context every render pass would fail to compile. Wrap the comparison in
vec4() like the other selectors fixed in the GL2 patchset.

Adaptation for the v7.387.0 rebase; not part of the 7.360.1 patchset.

=== 5 ===
gl2: polyfill round() for GLSL 1.20

Upstream 431c3170 ("renderer: dither onto the sample grid of the target",
between 7.360.1 and 7.387.0) snaps the output of every pass that renders
into a non-float target onto that texture's sample grid:

    color.rgba = round(color.rgba * 255.0) * 0.0039215688;

round() only exists from GLSL 1.30 on, so on a GL 2.x context the final
output pass of every frame fails to compile and mpv shows nothing but
a solid-colour window:

    ERROR: 0:90: 'round' : no matching overloaded function found
    ERROR: 0:90: 'assign' :  cannot convert from 'const float' to '4-component vector of float'
    Failed compiling/linking GLSL program
    Failed creating pass
    Failed rendering image!

Rather than patching this one call site, add round() to the GLSL < 130
compatibility prelude in dispatch.c, next to the texture()/textureLod()
mappings:

    #define round(x) floor((x) + 0.5)

floor(x + 0.5) rounds to nearest with ties going up, which the round()
specification permits, and floor() is overloaded for every genType just
like round(). This also covers the other round() users that can reach
a GLSL 1.20 target: the Dolby Vision NLQ enhancement-layer merge
(shaders/colorspace.c) and user shaders loaded through
pl_mpv_user_shader_parse(). GLSL >= 130 output is unchanged.

Observed on a GeForce 6600 (GL 2.0 NVIDIA-1.5.48, GLSL 1.20) with mpv
vo=gpu-next: solid magenta window, "Failed rendering frame!" on every
frame.

Adaptation for the v7.387.0 rebase; not part of the 7.360.1 patchset.

=== 6 ===
opengl: detect framebuffer object support on GL 2.x instead of forcing it

The GL2 backport unconditionally set has_fbos on every GL 2.0+ context,
with a note that extension detection was unreliable. That dated from
before the backport parsed GL_EXTENSIONS on contexts without
glGetStringi(); the extension list is reliable now (and is dumped to the
log), so test for GL_ARB_framebuffer_object / GL_EXT_framebuffer_object
like the GL 3.0+ path does, and warn if neither is there instead of
calling into NULL entry points.

GL 3.0+ and GLES 2.0+ keep FBOs unconditionally, as before. On GL 2.x the
EXT entry points are aliased onto the core names by pl_opengl_create().

Follow-up to the v7.387.0 rebase of the ppcports GL2 patchset.

=== 7 ===
opengl: enable 1D and 3D textures on GL 2.0 contexts

Upstream only advertises max_tex_1d_dim / max_tex_3d_dim from GL 2.1 on,
which for its purposes just means "any desktop GL". With the backport
accepting GL 2.0 contexts that left both limits at 0 on e.g. the macOS
GeForce 6/7 drivers, so every 1D LUT was stored as a 2D texture and 3D
LUTs (ICC profiles, the gamut mapping LUT, custom .cube LUTs) failed with
"Can't generate LUT: no compatible methods!". 1D textures are core since
GL 1.0 and 3D textures since GL 1.2, and the GLAD loader generated for
gl:compatibility=2.0 includes glTexImage1D/3D, so lower both thresholds
to 2.0.

Follow-up to the v7.387.0 rebase of the ppcports GL2 patchset.

=== 8 ===
shaders/deband: wrap the mix() selectors for GLSL 1.20

pl_shader_deband() picks between the averaged and the original sample
with

    res = mix(avg, res, greaterThan(diff, bound));
    res = mix(avg, res, diff > bound);

but mix() with a bool/bvec selector only exists from GLSL 1.30 on, so on
a GL 2.x context enabling debanding (mpv --deband) fails to compile the
pass. Wrap the comparisons in T()/float() like the other selectors fixed
in the GL2 patchset; the result is identical for finite values.

Follow-up to the v7.387.0 rebase of the ppcports GL2 patchset.

=== 9 ===
gl2: confine the FBO-format and LUT-uniform heuristics to GLSL < 130

Two tweaks from the GL2 backport changed behaviour on every backend:

- find_fbo_format() fell back to the 4-component FBO format before the
  next narrower one, to dodge legacy GL 2.x drivers that cannot render to
  the 3-component formats they advertise. On Vulkan / GL 3+ that only
  costs bandwidth, so apply it on GLSL < 130 only and restore upstream's
  fallback order elsewhere.
- sh_lut() kept 256 components of uniform headroom when deciding whether
  a LUT fits into uniforms, because old drivers report small
  max_variable_comps limits. Keep the headroom for GLSL < 130, use
  upstream's exact limit otherwise.

merge_fmt() requiring PL_FMT_CAP_RENDERABLE stays unconditional: the
merged plane is always rendered into, so a non-renderable merge format
could never have worked on any backend.

Follow-up to the v7.387.0 rebase of the ppcports GL2 patchset.

=== 10 ===
gl2: cleanups: debug-level setup messages, dither fallback, unused variable

- opengl/formats, renderer: the format-path, format-count and FBO-format
  messages added by the backport were logged at PL_INFO on every renderer
  (re)configuration. They are diagnostics, so log them at PL_DEBUG like
  the surrounding upstream code.
- shaders/dithering: the ORDERED_FIXED -> WHITE_NOISE downgrade for
  GLSL < 130 was checked twice, once at the LUT fallback label and once
  after it. Keep the single check after `done:`, which also covers
  callers requesting ORDERED_FIXED directly, and restore upstream's
  fallback label.
- opengl/gpu_tex: drop the unused `p` in gl_tex_clear_ex(), the one
  compiler warning from the patchset.

Follow-up to the v7.387.0 rebase of the ppcports GL2 patchset.

